# s3-09 -> CORE-WIRE-G2

- `native/core/crates/mixdog-tools/src/desktop/mod.rs`, after `mod computer_act;` (alphabetical, before `pub mod computer_backend;`):
  `mod computer_app_owned;`
- No Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock or workspace-hack edit: the module uses only crates mixdog-tools already depends on
  (async-trait, futures, mixdog-core-api, mixdog-js, mixdog-rt, serde_json, tokio-util; tokio test-util for the paused clock).
- No compose call and no protocol row: `host/computer/appWindows` and `host/computer/appInput` are core->host requests registered by the desktop side
  (their rows belong to s3-02), so SERVICE_PENDING gets no removal from this task.
- For s3-18 (act wiring, owns computer_act.rs / computer_backend.rs): in `send_step`, after `computer_frames::map_step`, when `delivery != "foreground"`:
  `APP_OWNED.route(&step, window_id)` -> `Some((window, op))` sends `app_input(desktop, &self.config.session_id, window_id, op, cancel)`; its `Ok(Value)` object is the step's result
  (same shape as a helper result); `Err(e)` with `computer_app_owned::falls_back(&e)` goes on to the helper path (today's behaviour); other errors fail the step.
  `preflight` must leave out the key/type steps `route` takes (`canUseAppOwnedInput` + `isAppOwnedWindow`). Remove the `#[allow(dead_code)]` markers of computer_app_owned.rs once wired.
  `computer_internal_windows::filter` already refreshes `APP_OWNED` with the internal ids on each list_windows / window_snapshot reply; the backend should also call
  `APP_OWNED.refresh(desktop.as_ref(), cancel)` (or `refresh_with(|| self.ask_desktop(WINDOWS_METHOD, ..))`) before routing a step when no list was read in the call.
- Contract assumed of the desktop (s3-02 must match): `appInput` params `{sessionThreadId, windowId, op, keys?, text?, x?, y?, button?, clicks?, dx?, dy?}` with points in physical px relative to the window's bounds;
  `keys` is the helper grammar of `normalizeComputerKeySequence` (what `electronKeyPresses` reads); `dx`/`dy` are signed CSS pixels (notches x 100, as `wheelDeltas`); `type` may carry `x`,`y` (the point the
  editable-target probe is run at after the preparatory click the desktop makes itself); answer `{delivered, effect: delivered|not_editable|window_gone|refused, evidence?, cursor?}`; -32602 when the window is not app-owned.
